{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes","id":1273272,"title":"VtM and Lovecraftian themes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-07T09:16:34-08:00","id":1273272,"title":"VtM and Lovecraftian themes","content":"How would you incorporate Lovecraftian themes into a VtM game that uses the Tremere?<br /> The WoD presents a great deal of magic, and some of that is infernalism. But the infernalism relates to fairly typical demons, fallen angels, and similar creatures. This is tonally different that Lovecraftian magic and themes.<br /> What are your thoughts on incorporating Loecraftian themes into a VtM game? How would you do it? Would it just be a name change, or something deeper?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T09:32:55-08:00","id":1273274,"title":"","content":"I think it would relate more to presenting the Abyss in a different tone. Lovecraft stuff focuses on cosmic horror and the unknown, so you want to emphasize them being out of their depth. Far reaching implications, but a degree of uncertainty. Highlighting their insignificance, degrees of hopelessness, insanity, and dread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T09:47:56-08:00","id":1273276,"title":"","content":"The Antediluvians often have a very Cthulhu vibe to them.<br /> <br /> That said, it depends a lot on which Lovecraft theme/tone you're going for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T11:27:39-08:00","id":1273288,"title":"","content":"I think Lovecraftian horror is both rather easy and pretty hard in Vampire at the same time.<br /> <br /> What are typical themes? The alien, the unknowable, the things-that-shouldn't-exist, existence defying natural law, maddening lore, the knowledge that humanity is just a footnote in someone else's story. Combine that with alien realms, dilapidated mansions, degenerated communities, tentacles and body horror and you've got Lovecraft.<br /> <br /> In other words: Lasombra and Tzimisce. Full stop.<br /> <br /> And on the other hand side, they're also what makes Lovecraftian horror so difficult, because the two clans are part of the Core 13. Every player who has read the VRev or V20 corebooks knows who they are, what they believe and what they usually do. And thus, when Lovecraftian horror requires the alien, the two have become mundane.<br /> <br /> Removing the two from the V5 core and reshaping the Sabbat from a massive faction with territories into a roving bogeyman may have been a step towards reestablishing their other-ness, but of course, that likely won't work on veteran players, depending on how much the two clans are changed. We'll find out when they reappear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3118,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","user":"Cifer","date":". 12-07-2018, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T13:31:05-08:00","id":1273304,"title":"","content":"I would agree with Michael that the Antediluvians and certain Methuselahs (as in, the direct childer of Antediluvians) would be the closest thing to approaching Lovecraftian horror. They are so old and so inhuman as to be completely alien to humanity today; in this respect, they're not so different from the &quot;Old Ones&quot; from the Cthulu Mythos. They have cults that worship them, even though they themselves seem to want little more than to end the world when they awake. What's worse, they're essentially unkillable; anything that would kill them would mean the end of the world. Obviously, this sounds exactly the Antediluvians, especially Set, but to a certain extent Haqim and Saulot too.<br /> <br /> You mentioned the Tremere... Well, that clan is probably the Lovecraftian of all because they're (1) the occult nerds clan and (2) their founder has literally been taken over by an Antediluvian, Saulot. The underlying storyline of your chronicle could be &quot;Tremere&quot; directing the Council (and by extension the PCs) to do certain things in motion that would help &quot;Tremere&quot; awaken and return to full power, but (duh) &quot;Tremere&quot; is Saulot. In one of the books (I think CB Tremere Revised) it's stated that &quot;Tremere&quot; presently takes the form of a giant gyrating white worm, which is itself pretty Lovecraftian.<br /> <br /> Cifer mentioned the Tzimisce... Also very Lovecraftian, and their Antediluvian is also around, underneath New York City, itself a living and alien monstrosity. The Tzimisce also have an ancestral grudge against the Tremere, so you could very well interweave the Tzimisce (not just the clan, but the Antediluvian itself) into the storyline. Saulot may seek the Tzimisce Antediluvian as an ally against Tremere since they both have reasons to want the Tremere wiped out.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I personally think Werewolf is better for &quot;cosmic horror&quot; stories, because that's the very nature of the Wyrm and Banes. Vampire was originally geared more toward &quot;personal horror&quot; (the very opposite of cosmic horror) but that changed as WW developed the Caine and Book of Nod stuff, and then the Final Nights/Gehenna. But by all means you can certainly do a very satisfying chronicle directly pulling in the Antediluvians and using them in a Lovecraftian way; in fact, I think that's the only way to handle them if you're going to use them. You certainly can't treat them as any normal NPC.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I am a prophet. I bring chaos and unrest to the foolish and wicked. I am no fit prince for Cainites, and I am no fit shepherd for the souls of men.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24720-anatole","name":"Anatole","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T14:02:38-08:00","id":1273312,"title":"","content":"Well, the obvious answer is the Baali and the Children.<br /> <br /> I feel like using the Lasombra and Tzimisce isn't actually going to help HPL because they're different sorts of evil to Lovecraft.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce is Lumleyian Evil.<br /> <br /> Lasombra are a kind of dark Catholicism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T14:24:00-08:00","id":1273321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1273312#post1273312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the obvious answer is the Baali and the Children.<br /> <br /> I feel like using the Lasombra and Tzimisce isn't actually going to help HPL because they're different sorts of evil to Lovecraft.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce is Lumleyian Evil.<br /> <br /> Lasombra are a kind of dark Catholicism.</div> </div> </div> </div>But as Grumpy noted, infernalism in WOD is treated as much more mundane (Faustian) than the cosmic horrors of Lovecraft. In WOD you sell your soul to a demon. In the Cthulu Mythos, you go insane if you even peek over the mountain's horizon, etc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I am a prophet. I bring chaos and unrest to the foolish and wicked. I am no fit prince for Cainites, and I am no fit shepherd for the souls of men.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24720-anatole","name":"Anatole","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T14:31:03-08:00","id":1273323,"title":"","content":"Two of the recurring themes of Lovecraft's works is the general insignificance of human beings and that his protagonists tend to detached, reclusive and socially isolated. This actually works pretty well with aspects of Vampire, in which the PCs would feel increasingly isolated from living humans, and start to see them as less and less important as they go deeper into the world of the Damned. Human contacts and avenues of influence gradually come to be seen as faceless pawns, and the general public as little more than a food source. In a lot of ways, being one of the Kindred is like finding out that you're actually descended from the Deep Ones, Ghouls or the Tcho Tcho.<br /> <br /> Another theme is a sense of hopelessness. Even when the protagonists succeed, it tends to be temporary and often comes with a high price to be paid later. (A prime example is &quot;The Call of Cthulhu&quot;, in which Johansen drives Cthulhu back into R'lyeh by ramming it in the head with a boat, only to later be murdered by cultists.) In Vampire, one of the biggest examples of this is the ongoing struggle between Humanity and the Beast. Any success to hold on to one's Humanity is ultimately futile, with Humanity inevitably eroding in the face of the endless moral challenges and compromises the Damned have to make just to survive. In addition, no matter how high one climbs among the Kindred, they'll still be at the mercy of Elders and Methuselah. This culminates with the potential doom that is Gehenna.<br /> <br /> Tied into this is the theme of how fragile sanity is. Many of the things Lovecraft's protagonists discover and witness are extraordinary if not incomprehensible to human beings. The strain of trying to cope can be impossible, and insanity is the result. In Vampire, you can see this in the insanity that often accompanies Humanity loss. The ugly truths of the Beast's inevitable triumph, the brutal existence of the Damned, and the separation from the living all take their toll. On top of this comes the unwanted knowledge of the secret puppet masters behind society and the existence of immortal monsters, including ghosts, demons and other creatures. Lovecraft also has a recurring theme of the protagonists never being able to fully understand what's going on and being left with unanswered questions. Vampire characters very well may never really understand the truth behind things like the Antediluvians, Caine, the true origins of vampires, Golcanda, the machinations of Methuselahs or Elders, True Faith, where the Daughters of Cacophony come from, etc. (An irony is that the Malkavians, who are driven insane by their embrace and clan curse, seem to have an instinctive insight into some of these unwelcome truths, which might actually help protect them from further mental degradation.)<br /> <br /> A lesser recurring surface detail is Lovecraft's slightly antiquarian writing style and his preference for British spellings. Vampire plays on this, with ancilla and elders often being behind the curve with technology and culture.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 12-07-2018, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T14:46:58-08:00","id":1273328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anatole</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1273321#post1273321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But as Grumpy noted, infernalism in WOD is treated as much more mundane (Faustian) than the cosmic horrors of Lovecraft. In WOD you sell your soul to a demon. In the Cthulu Mythos, you go insane if you even peek over the mountain's horizon, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but the Baali aren't treated as Infernalist in their handbook.<br /> <br /> Their goal is to keep the Sleeping God-Demons asleep.<br /> <br /> Not to make deals with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T14:54:22-08:00","id":1273331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1273312#post1273312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the obvious answer is the Baali and the Children.<br /> <br /> I feel like using the Lasombra and Tzimisce isn't actually going to help HPL because they're different sorts of evil to Lovecraft.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce is Lumleyian Evil.<br /> <br /> Lasombra are a kind of dark Catholicism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, in Tome of Secrets, Lasombra come off quite 'edlritch horrors of the Abyss' than 'dark Catholicism'. Baali aren't necessarily a bad direction. But really, I think any can do fine, it just needs certain presentation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T15:23:04-08:00","id":1273338,"title":"","content":"This is kinda what I was referring to by asking what tone or theme we're actually talking about. There's arguably a certain level of 'Dark Christianity' to Lovecraft.<br /> <br /> The underlying issue is that Lovecraft wrote stories with quite different styles of horror to them but which refer back on each other and reinterpret themselves. So for example, The Call of Cthulhu does the whole insignificance of Humanity thing straight, then later we get At the Mountains of Madness where we see the same theme again perhaps even more explicitly, but the narrator doubles back on it and ultimately empathises with the Elder Things.<br /> <br /> I think there's potentially a useful parallel between the city in At the Mountains of Madness and Enoch. Assume something clears out the True Black Hand and go from there, exploring a ruin trying to work out what happened to the inhabitants before it happens to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T16:20:05-08:00","id":1273345,"title":"","content":"The obvious path with the Tremere is the dawning horror that they are, in fact, a bloodline of the Tzimisce and, therefore, progeny of a cursed heritage. Alienage was a big... and problematic... theme in HPL's fiction. Have the pcs discover the whole &quot;Tzimisce are nothing but extensions of the Eldest's body and will&quot; lore, then have them realize they themselves are also part of the collective. Ticks a lot of HPL boxes.<br /> <br /> The less obvious way to play it is with Malkav. The Tremere have Auspex, and a habit of looking into things better left undiscovered. If you assume that Madness (not just garden variety mental illness), is a palpable force as real and inexorable as gravity, gathers in eddies and currents, and is always seeking a new host, then the Malkavians become more than just bunny slipper wearing fools. They become the heralds of an ancient evil which eats away your mind and, indeed, your very soul. Malkavians, as a clan, could easily be portrayed as the servant race of their Ante. The pcs must risk contact with the Lunatics to fight them, but <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/InfectiousInsanity\" target=\"_blank\">each contact risks deeper infection</a> with the mental corrosion inflicted by the Ante.<br /> <br /> Picture Village of the Damned, the Crazies, or even Jasmine from the Angel tv series. Canon was fumbling towards this portrayal with Dementation, but never really managed to lose the bunny slippers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T16:23:31-08:00","id":1273346,"title":"","content":"There used to be a theory that Dementation <i>was</i> Malkav.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T18:29:38-08:00","id":1273362,"title":"","content":"I think a big thing to note is the themes of Vampire: The Masquerade and HP Lovecraft are related but sometimes contradictory. Being a vampire is about your humanity being lost and the horrors of losing your humanity while the horror of HPL is that humanity itself is insigificant as well as unimportant so does V:TM make it all important.<br /> <br /> If I were to make it a Lovecraftian work, I would have the vampires deal with people's shock and existential horror from the perspective of mortals.<br /> <br /> They are the monsters in the night so human Touchstones or associates seeing the truth of reality and being driven insane by the results or suicidal is a case.<br /> <br /> Another good use would be Revenants who have the &quot;cursed blood&quot; thing going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T18:48:33-08:00","id":1273366,"title":"","content":"You can always include incidental elements to the game that are Lovecraftian. If your WoD is influenced by cosmic horror (as my chronicles are) then they can seep in anywhere. Although Vampire is probably the game that is least susceptible to those elements because so much of the game is recursive - vampires interact with other vampires, unlike the other game lines where the PCs routinely encounter people and creatures unlike themselves.<br /> <br /> However, the easiest way to introduce thematic appropriate Lovecraftian elements is to think of what exactly the antedeluvian world was like. Although the books base it on Christian mythology, there is absolutely no reason why there can't have been a real antedeluvian world, but one based on the works of the old masters (Lovecraft, Smith, Howard) and others. Maybe the antedeluvian world where vampirism was born was Atlantis and &quot;Cain&quot; was the head of a sorcerous cabal with the clan founders as his disciples, and they inadvertently created vampirism (the canonical origin of vampires in the Marvel Universe is very similar to this). Then when vampires go on Noddist explorations, they encounter artifacts and lore that introduce cosmic horror.<br /> <br /> And of course if you have cosmic horror &quot;gods&quot; and such, any occult oriented PCs are going to run into that along with the more familiar infernalism. How well you blend those various elements together just depends on your skill. But it has been in Hellboy and the Dresden Files among many others. So you can look at them for inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T19:20:44-08:00","id":1273371,"title":"","content":"Mind you, I think it's perfectly fine to also have Cosmic Horror as a backdrop to personal horror.<br /> <br /> Are the Eldrtich Things in addition to God or is God a thing vampires made up?<br /> <br /> Or are they existing simultaneously perhaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T19:55:49-08:00","id":1273375,"title":"","content":"You could do something like The Rats in the Wall. Short story shorter: a community in prehistoric England started domesticating and breeding other humans into livestock to eat and this went on until the 17th century. They lived under a temple/priory/manor. Vampires might do something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T20:09:21-08:00","id":1273378,"title":"","content":"In the old supplement, &quot;Dark Colony&quot; the chronicle in the book was an attempt at incorporating Lovecraftian elements into Vampire in a fitting setting for both: New England. It even featured a Tremere antagonist summoning an eldritch entity ( a Nexus Crawler of werewolf). I suggest that you don't define it in character or out of character; don't put the entities in an understandable framework or define it in a manner that allows the players to neatly provide context to it or quantify it (&quot;Oh, it's a Type VI demon!&quot;). For example, there's no need to ever use the term &quot;Nexus Crawler&quot; or connect the entity to any particular mythos. Don't provide exposition. Neither confirm nor deny; and never give them &quot;the answer&quot;. I'd also make it so the worse atrocities are committed by the very human cultists who serve the &quot;dark powers&quot; or whatever, keep the vampire remote, requiring work to see what lurks behind the mortals, and then what lurks behind the vampire..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24582-ruthven","name":"Ruthven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T20:36:18-08:00","id":1273381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruthven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1273378#post1273378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the old supplement, &quot;Dark Colony&quot; ...</div> </div> </div> </div>How is this supplement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T00:06:41-08:00","id":1273403,"title":"","content":"The plot of the game Bloodborne, specifically regarding the School of Mensis, is pretty much an easy 1 to 1 lift to create a Lovecraftian Tremere story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2763-nunboi","name":"nunboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2763_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T16:20:50-08:00","id":1273508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1273381#post1273381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How is this supplement?</div> </div> </div> </div>The supplement as a whole, well, average to slightly below average. There's a &quot;British Kindred&quot; vs. &quot;American Kindred&quot; ala the revolutionary war that comes across too thick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24582-ruthven","name":"Ruthven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T16:21:48-08:00","id":1273509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1273323#post1273323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two of the recurring themes of Lovecraft's works is the general insignificance of human beings and that his protagonists tend to detached, reclusive and socially isolated...</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. Gotta remember the eldritch horrors were never really the point. Running a game where PC's are Tremere neonates simply learning to navigate the Pyramid is plenty Lovecraftian at its core. Remember the nature of the clan and the Pyramid.<br /> <br /> Literally everyone hates and fears the Tremere, especially the Tremere. For most Tremere neonates who don't get the privilege of working with external coteries, the Pyramid is all they have. Of course, the Pyramid is a cult of personality working under a perpetual siege mentality, which is a serpents' nest of backbiting, lies, betrayal, and utter obsession with the will to power that well surpasses even that of the Lasombra, all bound by supernaturally-enforced oaths of loyalty, propaganda, supernatural gaslighting, and indoctrination, when the reality is the only <i>real</i> rule is &quot;don't get caught&quot;. In fact, in a certain point of view the Lasombra are the Tremere's moral superiors, because at least they're <i>honest</i> about their internal strife and constant backstabbing, and make it well known from the very onset with zero room for misinterpretation that in the final analysis, each and every Lasombra stands alone.<br /> <br /> But, the linchpin is, the Pyramid mandates all Tremere maintain their Humanity to preserve the Masquerade. For any vampire, in the long run this is a fool's errand, but in this regard the Tremere are uniquely set up to fail, and catastrophically at that.<br /> <br /> Common restrictions as mandated by Tremere siege mentality, upon neonates and apprentices at large, tends toward limiting contact with mortals -- after all, a Tremere outside the walls of their chantry is a vulnerable Tremere. Meanwhile, to simply use Thaumaturgy requires one unlearn everything they may or may not know about metaphysics, and put in its place a Medieval worldview that is foreign and alien to the post-Enlightenment mind, and this process of changing one's worldview is <i>readily</i> supplemented by mind control, torture, and other abuses should it not proceed to the Regent's liking. This is a discipline all Tremere are <b><i>required</i></b> to learn to the near-exclusion of all else, with exceptions few and far between for Tremere whose sole decreed purpose is to manage the clan's assets and act as liaisons to the mortal world. Then comes the actual practice of Thaumaturgy, which can and does require activities like theft, vandalism, graverobbing, consent violation, torture, even murder, at its upper echelons of use. Make no mistake, to learn and practice Thaumaturgy regularly is a strain on Humanity that cannot be easily borne in the short term, and in the long term becomes impossible.<br /> <br /> And, as I alluded to earlier, this is <i>all by design</i>. The Tremere are only as strong as their weakest link, and as such they have zero tolerance or sympathy for weakness. Every last aspect of the Pyramid is purpose-built by some of the most intelligent and strategically-minded beings to have ever existed, to destroy everything neonates ever were, and may have ever been, to recreate them in the clan's own image in the face of an entire world that would destroy them to their last without hesitation or remorse given half a chance.<br /> <br /> Is it any wonder so many go rogue, turn to infernalism, eventually go mad, or degenerate too rapidly and have to be reprogrammed or destroyed? In an entire game and setting awash with Lovecraftian themes, the Tremere are a cut above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 12-08-2018, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T18:22:21-08:00","id":1273526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1273371#post1273371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, I think it's perfectly fine to also have Cosmic Horror as a backdrop to personal horror.<br /> <br /> Are the Eldrtich Things in addition to God or is God a thing vampires made up?<br /> <br /> Or are they existing simultaneously perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>HPL's universe didn't have God, at least not in the traditional sense of an omnipotent, omniscient, benevolent infinite-being who created, sustains, and intervenes in the universe.<br /> <br /> Not to get too theological, but a God who is in any sense infinite would need to be infinite in all Their qualities. A good God would need to be infinitely good. By definition, if God created the universe They created everything within the universe, including the Great Old Ones. Being infinitely omniscient, God would have actively and consciously chosen to set in motion the events which proceed from the creation of them. Yep, the whole Lovecraftian mythos from the Deep Ones right up to Azathoth would need to be actively part of God's plan. The human cultists retain free-will, and responsibility, one presumes... with the usual Calvinist and Barthian predestination asterisks.<br /> <br /> The reconciliation for &quot;a benevolent God in a world that includes evil&quot; is one of the denser problems in theology.<br /> <br /> Then there's the narrative problem of what story element the players would interact with to confirm or deny the cosmology of the storyline. Such high-level cosmology is probably neither a necessary nor a helpful piece of world-building. (Admittedly, it is a fun topic for musing about a built world.)<br /> <br /> But, then what do I know? I'm a lapsed Unitarian, and you don't get much more lapsed than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T20:18:31-08:00","id":1273541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1273526#post1273526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> HPL's universe didn't have God, at least not in the traditional sense of an omnipotent, omniscient, benevolent infinite-being who created, sustains, and intervenes in the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually what I'm getting at. V:TM is Judeo-Christian horror that relies on being damned before a legalistic but theoretically just God.<br /> <br /> Lovecraft is about being doomed by an uncaring and empty universe.<br /> <br /> [quot]Not to get too theological, but a God who is in any sense infinite would need to be infinite in all Their qualities. A good God would need to be infinitely good. By definition, if God created the universe They created everything within the universe, including the Great Old Ones. Being infinitely omniscient, God would have actively and consciously chosen to set in motion the events which proceed from the creation of them. Yep, the whole Lovecraftian mythos from the Deep Ones right up to Azathoth would need to be actively part of God's plan. The human cultists retain free-will, and responsibility, one presumes... with the usual Calvinist and Barthian predestination asterisks.[/quote]<br /> <br /> Mind you, there's also the Revelations of the Dark Mother where God is just first among the Elohim and thus not omnipotent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The reconciliation for &quot;a benevolent God in a world that includes evil&quot; is one of the denser problems in theology. </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. It depends on whether or not you accept the answer.<br /> <br /> But I include a lot of Lovecraftian mythology in my games, sometimes while including Judeo-Christian and the following answers have been used:<br /> <br /> * The Great Old Ones of the setting are the fallen Archdemons in the Underworld. I.e. the take from Demon: The Fallen. It's a very Christian take but there's the possible horrifying fact God has left or died which leaves only the alien Cthulhuoid insane entities.<br /> <br /> * The Great Old Ones are the &quot;things before the Light&quot; and are chaotic horrifying beings that are not part of God's law or universe. God defeated them with Lucifer leading the host against them.<br /> <br /> * God in the V:TM world is a product of human faith and not the reverse. The GOO are the true gods of the universe.<br /> <br /> * The GOO are the Wyrm's various faces. &quot;God&quot; is either the Patriarch or a somewhat more benevolent face of Jupiter or Helios.<br /> <br /> * God is one of the &quot;young gods&quot; who was created by Gaia and the Elder Gods are the things before Gaia (which is actually the history of the Marvel Universe's magical entities by Roy Thomas).<br /> <br /> * The GOO actually are simply aliens from another world that have come to the Earth. They have their own gods and are far older than our own.<br /> <br /> * God is actually Azathoth, purely driven by wild and animalistic urges, but humans have ascribed mortal ideas to it. His power is real but it answers to whoever who channels it, good or evil.<br /> <br /> * God is one of many gods like Zeus, Odin, and others. Their numbers dwindle now and the fight is only kept up by Oracles of the Mages, Changelings, and others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-08-2018, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T20:36:10-08:00","id":1273544,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, as others have pointed out, Lovecraftian Horror is about Cosmic Horror - the insignificance of humanity (and especially of a single human) and the alien and inscrutable creatures that populate the world but are beyond any sort of human understanding.<br /> <br /> I've found one of the easiest ways to do that is to actually pull from stuff outside of VtM, such as grabbing Umbral spirits from Werewolf. They're peripherally part of the VtM cosmology, but are extremely alien and unknowable since outside of a small handful, vampires generally don't truck with those sort of creatures. Many of them are also totally inhuman and operate along concepts that are well outside of what humans might want. You can drop a corrupted Wyrm spirit into a game and boom, you've got unknowable cosmic horror represented by things that even supernatural monsters like vampires would find frightening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T05:22:35-08:00","id":1273576,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> <br /> <br /> Lots of cogent ideas there. How do you present the different versions to the players, in game? Or, is it out-of-character exposition presented informally away from the table?<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I've been meaning to read some of your books. I am <i>almost</i> caught up on my other reading. (Well, as much as I ever am.) Where would be a good place to start? Is there a particular order you suggest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T07:30:37-08:00","id":1273581,"title":"","content":"Methuselahs can be used to deliver Chtonic Horror pretty easily. Not every Meth is &quot;human&quot; like Mithras, or &quot;relatable&quot; like Helena and Menele.<br /> Yorak, Byelobog, Ur-Shulgi, Enkidu, the Hierophants, The Baali founders,Odin,the sire of Esperanza Lucifer,Lamdiel, Nissiku, the Word Eater, Tiamat and so on...they are all good examples of really out of touch creatures, inhuman and fathomless, and powerful beyond imagination.<br /> A thing like Yorak can be pretty much alien, and the Chatedral of Flesh doesn't have much to envy from Ryl'eh; Nissiku is so strange that he just warps reality and madness follows him like a plague; Tiamat is a Demon-Vampire that lies in the depth of ancient and forgotten tomb; Odin is an old necromancer that lead a cult of blood whose legacy still lives in the darkest nights of Norther Europe.<br /> <br /> Let your players being caught in the threads of the Jyhad, put multiple layer of complexity and horror, let them feel little and powerless in front of an old feud between alien beings that control society and history. Let them glimpse the horror beneath the city, ancient crypts lost in ages, blood rituals to appease the gods of old and so on.<br /> <br /> It's really easy, since the 2nd edition Vampire moved from personal horror to chtonic horror pretty quickly. You really don't have to use things from other settings, you already have everything you need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 12-09-2018, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T10:40:31-08:00","id":1273595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1273576#post1273576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a><br /> <br /> Lots of cogent ideas there. How do you present the different versions to the players, in game? Or, is it out-of-character exposition presented informally away from the table?<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I've been meaning to read some of your books. I am <i>almost</i> caught up on my other reading. (Well, as much as I ever am.) Where would be a good place to start? Is there a particular order you suggest?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, I have characters speculate on it in-universe. Baali, Tremere, old books, mages, Nephandi, and so on.<br /> <br /> You never have to give a definitive answer but the mere suggestion is terrifying by itself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T14:05:57-08:00","id":1273628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes#post1273272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are your thoughts on incorporating Loecraftian themes into a VtM game? How would you do it? Would it just be a name change, or something deeper?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could include a human ( maybe a Mage, maybe a mundane human ) who could be somebody who delves into lovecraftian matters and knowledge, or has encountered them ; this person would be based or inspired by some of the protagonists of H.P Lovecraft's stories. The PCs would get their first glimpse, information, and impressions about the lovecraftian matter at hand from this interactions with this person ( or her or his writings ) . After some interactions, they would have a choice what to do in regard to this person, and whether to investigate the introduced matter or knowledge further.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anatole</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1273304#post1273304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would agree with Michael that the Antediluvians and certain Methuselahs (as in, the direct childer of Antediluvians) would be the closest thing to approaching Lovecraftian horror. They are so old and so inhuman as to be completely alien to humanity today; in this respect, they're not so different from the &quot;Old Ones&quot; from the Cthulu Mythos. They have cults that worship them, even though they themselves seem to want little more than to end the world when they awake. What's worse, they're essentially unkillable; anything that would kill them would mean the end of the world. Obviously, this sounds exactly the Antediluvians, especially Set, but to a certain extent Haqim and Saulot too.<br /> <br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I much prefer for it to be that the 3rd Generation Founders are extremely capable, intelligent, and powerful, and can accomplish awesome feats, but are ultimately relatively comparable to other Vampires ( or other persons ) in regard to how they think and what motivates them. Of course some of them have very specific view points, perspectives, and approaches ; but for me this doesn't have to contradict them being comprehensible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T18:28:50-08:00","id":1273642,"title":"","content":"Another recurring theme in some of Lovecraft's work is that of inherited guilt, or the idea of the &quot;sins of the father being visited upon the son&quot;. This is a really common trope of classic Gothic literature and so is already a component of Vampire. The most common take being that Childer end up getting caught up in the machinations of their Sires and paying a pretty steep personal price. It also works really well with Ghouls and especially with Revenant families, and the Ventrue make for fertile ground as well. Back during 1st ed and part of the early 2nd, you'd see more than one Ventrue who was strongly tied to a single mortal family, be it his (it was usually a he) own or one where someone back in the day had become sworn to his service. The price for this is that, in addition to being the vampire's pawns or source of resources, the family may serve as a herd (especially for a Ventrue who can only feed on that bloodline) or young members discover that they're being groomed for the embrace. (The Giovanni are practically based around this idea.)<br /> <br /> Also, Lovecraft didn't exist in a vacuum. His own works were strongly influenced by the stories of Edgar Allan Poe, Arthur Machen, Robert Chambers, Algernon Blackwood and Lord Dunsany, all of whose works offer up potential ideas and themes that can be incorporated into Vampire. Dunsany's stories, which influenced Lovecraft's Dreamlands, can be inspiration for a group of Auspex-possessing vampires - especially Malkavians - astrally projecting into a dreamlike realm of strange beings and cryptic gods. Perhaps even bringing something back with them. I also recommend looking at some of the work's by Nathanial Hawthorne, especially for anyone who wants to set a Vampire game in New England. <br /> <br /> There's also Lovecraft's contemporaries who each built upon the Mythos in their own way. I find that Robert E Howard's works, especially his horror stories, work really well for Vampire games set out in the American West and for those that involve barbaric anachronisms released from torpor into the modern nights. Clark Ashton Smith's works tended to involve protagonists striving, often in vain, to recover some lost and idealized part of their past. This is perfect for Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 12-09-2018, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T07:57:44-08:00","id":1273720,"title":"","content":"One approach could be to have events happen that suggest a lovecraftian reason behind them, but ultimately have it revealed that it is not a case. And then an actual lovecraftian element(s) could be introduced separately afterwards.<br /> <br /> Another way to include lovecraftian elements is to do a crossover with M:tA and include the Nephandi from the K'llashaa Nephandi sub-faction. Though there is very, very little written about them in the M:tA books, so the storyteller would have to develop them further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T11:06:43-07:00","id":1486163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1273381#post1273381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How is this supplement?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's rather bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24582-ruthven","name":"Ruthven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T14:33:48-07:00","id":1486180,"title":"","content":"There's an expression I heard somewhere, though I know not where, that I think is related to Lovecraft: &quot;In New England, the old secrets are very secret. In Old England, the old secrets are very old.&quot;<br /> <br /> Vampires are both very secret and very old, though some are older and more secret than others. While the Tremere are certainly even more secretive, they aren't nearly as old as other vampires.<br /> <br /> This means that any given Tremere Neonate has the unenviable fortune to be nestled between very secret secrets, within their own Clan, and very old secrets, from without. There's no telling what those higher in the Pyramid have been doing, but Elder and Methuselah vampires outside the Pyramid have been doing strange and mysterious things for FAR longer.<br /> <br /> See, one of the underappreciated elements of vampires is just HOW old their oldest can be. And what that age really MEANS. Anyone can look at a number and think they understand what that age means. But in truth, no one is really prepared to reckon with Deep Time.<br /> <br /> No consider that, by the standards of Deep Time, vampires (at least according to Noddist thinking) are practically newborns. Assuming, of course, vampires are &quot;only&quot; 10,000 years old. A Lovecraftian Vampire campaign could easily challenge these assumptions, and present the idea that vampires, or their antecedents, have been around far longer than most can possibly imagine.<br /> <br /> Insert vampiric serpent people here. Taking tithes of blood amid cyclopean structures built in prehistory so old, humans themselves weren't even a glimmer of a possibility.<br /> <br /> A not-insubstantial number of impossibly ancient structures in Lovecraft's stories can be found beneath the waves. Modern humans have still, to this day, barely mapped the ocean floor. Lovecraft himself was likely unaware of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doggerland\" target=\"_blank\">Doggerland</a>, pre-Ice Age regions that once connected his beloved England to the continent. Who knows what could be hiding there? What <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Temple_(Lovecraft_short_story)\" target=\"_blank\">ancient temples</a>, what <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dagon_(short_story)\" target=\"_blank\">buried monoliths</a>, what <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Call_of_Cthulhu\" target=\"_blank\">sunken cities containing sleeping Great Ones</a>? More importantly, what sort of MAGIC might an aspiring blood sorcerer find in such places?<br /> <br /> Remember, vampires don't need to breathe, and are reasonably insulated from the effects of crushing (read: Bashing) ocean depths. Go down far enough, the sun doesn't even shine.<br /> <br /> Why, such an aspiring Tremere Neonate could just...GO DOWN THERE. There can't be that much that can harm an immortal vampire, down there. Right?<br /> <br /> (It's situations like this that <i>World of Darkness: Blood Dimmed Tides</i> becomes a useful resource.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T20:12:45-07:00","id":1486197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486180#post1486180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, vampires don't need to breathe, and are reasonably insulated from the effects of crushing (read: Bashing) ocean depths. Go down far enough, the sun doesn't even shine.<br /> <br /> Why, such an aspiring Tremere Neonate could just...GO DOWN THERE. There can't be that much that can harm an immortal vampire, down there. Right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Little curio for you:<br /> <br /> The idea that deep oceanic pressure would crush you is just a legend. It wouldn't. Even a normal human wouldn't die directly from the pressure.<br /> <br /> Of course, we <b>would</b> die, first because we would become unable to breath even with an oxygen tank (too much pressure to inflate the lungs), second because the pressure changes some chemical reactions and would turn the nitrogen in our blood into a poison (even more so during depressurization, actually).<br /> <br /> But vampires do not breath and do not bother with nitrogen bubbles in the blood. <b>There is no damage</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T23:24:21-07:00","id":1486208,"title":"","content":"For me, I think the best way to do Lovecraft in V:TM is the <b>Baali.</b><br /> <br /> The original Dark Ages supplement renvisioned the Baali as people who existed as tenders of the sleeping horrors beneath the waves. Demon: The Fallen had the view that these were Earthbound but you could very easily choose to renvision it as something else. Basically, Christians and other religions have given these things the names of demons or pagan gods but the truth is they're something...else.<br /> <br /> Indeed, this is actually Lovecraftian in itself as the SHADOW OVER INNSMOUTH was interpreted as Dagon being a different entity than Cthulhu but I always viewed it as them worshiping Cthulhu himself and giving him the Biblical fish god's name.<br /> <br /> V:TM is very Christian in its presentation, but there's something to be said for the idea of presenting that VAMPIRES HAVE IT COMPLETELY WRONG. The idea that vampirism is something wholly unrelated to a moral sinful universe and they're something &quot;else&quot; and also at the bottom of the totem pole.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T02:26:05-07:00","id":1486210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486208#post1486208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon: The Fallen had the view that these were Earthbound but you could very easily choose to renvision it as something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that never made any sense to begin with to be honest!<br /> The Children and the First Tribe of Ashur who tended them predated the summoning of the first Earthbounds by god know how many millenia<br /> Asmodeus was eventually summoned by a caste of royal magicians and mathematicians in Sumer.<br /> The palace of the Akkadians, home of King Sargon, was prepared by a select group of priestesses known as the Ur-Dalla, or the \u201cSisterhood of the Needle.\u201d The marble floor of the palace was soaked in the blood of animal sacrifices, the carcasses ripe and festering as Abaddon\u2019s soul was dragged into the reliquary, becoming one of the first Earthbound.<br /> Azrael was summoned by the necromancer kings of Kush, who had constructed a temple of bone and bodies to glorify the archduke.<br /> Belial was summoned by the court magicians of the Shang Dynasty in China, with offerings of jade, silk and thousand immolated bodies. - The Shang ruled from 1600 to 1046 B.C<br /> The first civilizations in the Indus valley discovered Dagons Name, constructed his reliquary and called him by the sound of a thousand hammers falling on gore-encrusted bronze bells, a ritual carried out by a mindless cult of insane architects. Dagon relocated to the city of Mohenjo-Daro, where he was worshipped as &quot;Arumukam the Six-Faced&quot;.<br /> Supposedly, they were summoned around the same time, and more or less together<br /> <br /> But the main problem with that theory is, Namtaru and the other Children had... have bodies, and one of their member were excavated and burnt under the Sun, since they are the Children of Darkness, existed before God commanded: Let there be light!<br /> <br /> Logically, the Childen can't be the Earthbounds... but something way older.<br /> Even before time existed, just only Darkness... like Grandmother (Grand Maw) of the Wraith/Orpheus or the Chulorviah<br /> They are however the best Lovercraftian nightmares of WoD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T08:17:02-07:00","id":1486225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486208#post1486208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, I think the best way to do Lovecraft in V:TM is the <b>Baali.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>There are so many ways to introduce Lovecraftian themes in the game, you're going to the path of least resistance?<br /> <br /> Even the authors had selected other ways to officially deal with such themes. The Abyss of Obtenebration, the Souleaters, secret societies within the Tremere and other clans, the things the Nosferatu sometimes encounter in the depths of the earth.<br /> <br /> Lovecraftian themes aren't just about serving entities with weird names, it is about finding out that your entire society and world view is ultimately meaningless in the face of an uncaring universe whose span in space and time is unfathomable, inhabited by beings to whom we're less than a passing fad.<br /> <br /> Much like the real universe, but through the eyes of a guy afraid of air conditioners and with mad writing skillz.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486208#post1486208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, this is actually Lovecraftian in itself as the SHADOW OVER INNSMOUTH was interpreted as Dagon being a different entity than Cthulhu but I always viewed it as them worshiping Cthulhu himself and giving him the Biblical fish god's name.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're better at Lovecraft than Lovecraft? There's a lot to unpack here.<br /> <br /> First, Dagon is not a &quot;biblical fish god&quot;, it is not a fish god on the bible and insisting on using the bible as &quot;primary source&quot; for religions of other peoples is offensive.<br /> <br /> Dagon, or Dagan, was a god in ancient Summer and Mesopotamia. He was a &quot;Father of Gods&quot; type, also a god of prosperity and kingship. The bible cites Dagon as the main god of the Philistines, only that and several times, although actual research indicates this probably wasn't true as there's no evidence of his worship in Canaan whatsoever, that's probably a later conflation with their contact with Mesopotamia.<br /> <br /> The &quot;fish-god&quot; nonsense came up in the 11th century as an erroneous etymology tracing his name to a Hebrew word for fish, and was taken for granted because the bible is always right and no one cares, later any figure of fish or fish-people in Summerian ruins were taken as evidence of the link, but those figure are actually another entity from their mythology with no ties to Dagon.<br /> <br /> Lovecraft obviously didn't know any of that and went with the fish-god wagon. But he wrote about Dagon in more places than just &quot;the Shadow Over Innsmouth&quot;, including a previous piece titled &quot;Dagon&quot;, and approved writings of others who also wrote about Dagon as its own entity.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing, Cthulhu wasn't the only or the most important entity in the Mythos, that was never the point. Lovecraft wrote about alien entities of unfathomable power like Yog-Sothot, about common legends and religions sometimes hiding alien horrors like Dagon, about advanced races without any resemblance to humans messing with us, like Elder Things and Yithians, about normal humans being corrupted and alienated by dark practices like Herbert West or the De La Poer family, and above all the casual ease of those horrors intrusion in human lives, like the Dunwitch Horror, Nyarlathotep or the dream quests that risk bringing real monsters to the world after just a wrong turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486208#post1486208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V:TM is very Christian in its presentation, but there's something to be said for the idea of presenting that VAMPIRES HAVE IT COMPLETELY WRONG. The idea that vampirism is something wholly unrelated to a moral sinful universe and they're something &quot;else&quot; and also at the bottom of the totem pole.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Lovecraft 101 and the authors already dropped hints of that nature across the books for anyone who wants to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T08:27:56-07:00","id":1486226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486210#post1486210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that never made any sense to begin with to be honest!</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you take everything at face value, which isn't how the setting is supposed to work.<br /> <br /> The Children and the Earthbound may not be the same entities. Or the account in Dark Ages may be wrong, as the Baali have conflicting accounts all over the place. Or the descriptions of the summoning of the Earthbound is a lie. There are many possibilities.<br /> <br /> While as an option I think the Children work fine as Lovecraftian horrors that predate everything else, to state that one account doesn't make sense because you're taking another at face value is naive, and closes possibilities for other people that may prefer other routes to deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T12:26:21-07:00","id":1486235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486226#post1486226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Children and the Earthbound may not be the same entities. Or the account in Dark Ages may be wrong, as the Baali have conflicting accounts all over the place. Or the descriptions of the summoning of the Earthbound is a lie. There are many possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>The various conflicting Baali origins, and methods of why they do what they do is the ultimate version of having you look at the left hand and not noticing what the right hand is doing...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T15:36:11-07:00","id":1486240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486225#post1486225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're better at Lovecraft than Lovecraft? There's a lot to unpack here.<br /> <br /> First, Dagon is not a &quot;biblical fish god&quot;, it is not a fish god on the bible and insisting on using the bible as &quot;primary source&quot; for religions of other peoples is offensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I hate to cut you off here but I know you realize that Dagon is actually described as both a Biblical Fish God and namesake for Cthulhu in the Shadow Over Innsmouth. The thing is: so do I.<br /> <br /> I am aware of the primary source of the religion but that absolutely NOTHING to do with the Shadow over Innsmouth. I'm purely referring to its use in fiction.<br /> <br /> You are equating the historical mythological figure with a demonic space alien. Something I think we both agree here is morally incorrect. I think it's important to ABSOLUTELY draw a wall between the two concepts and to equate the two is a terrible idea. It's akin to attempting to add more historical elements of the religion of Nergal to the Baali. Which is self-defeating because the demonic reinvisioning of real life mythological figures is a terrible and offensive idea.<br /> <br /> It's why I always state, &quot;vampires never are the primary source of a religion. They can IMPERSONATE said religious figures [and often do] but should never be the actual figures.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mind you, this has problems with Mithras and Set but it's how I feel. Don't ever say anyone else's gods were demons. I think you're misreading my view that I think Lovecraft's use of Dagon as a name for Cthulhu has anything to do with the real life religion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing, Cthulhu wasn't the only or the most important entity in the Mythos, that was never the point. Lovecraft wrote about alien entities of unfathomable power like Yog-Sothot, about common legends and religions sometimes hiding alien horrors like Dagon, about advanced races without any resemblance to humans messing with us, like Elder Things and Yithians, about normal humans being corrupted and alienated by dark practices like Herbert West or the De La Poer family, and above all the casual ease of those horrors intrusion in human lives, like the Dunwitch Horror, Nyarlathotep or the dream quests that risk bringing real monsters to the world after just a wrong turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Dagon IS Cthulhu in The Shadow over Innsmouth.<br /> <br /> That's my point.<br /> <br /> The Deep Ones are not worshiping Dagon the historical mythological figure, they are worshiping Cthulhu but applying (erroneously) the name of a god they're familiar with as a fundamentalist Christian educated town from the 19th century to early 20th.<br /> <br /> My post is suggesting the Baali could be doing the same thing and adding the names of angels and other figures to alien things from beyondTM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-11-2022, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T19:32:01-07:00","id":1486250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486240#post1486240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am aware of the primary source of the religion but that absolutely NOTHING to do with the Shadow over Innsmouth. I'm purely referring to its use in fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was not what your phrasing seemed to suggest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486240#post1486240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's important to ABSOLUTELY draw a wall between the two concepts and to equate the two is a terrible idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's exactly why I explained their difference instead of just saying &quot;giving him the Biblical fish god's name&quot; and stopping at that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486240#post1486240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are equating the historical mythological figure with a demonic space alien.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't said anything to this effect in my post and I <b>am </b>taking personal offense with this statement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486240#post1486240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're misreading my view that I think Lovecraft's use of Dagon as a name for Cthulhu has anything to do with the real life religion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But Dagon IS Cthulhu in The Shadow over Innsmouth.<br /> <br /> That's my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your point is wrong.<br /> <br /> Lovecraft used the name Dagon for the same reason most fiction authors use the name Dagon, referring to that old (and wrong) notion of Dagon as a fish-god, and a Demon because for him and many others, any foreign god described in the bible is a demon.<br /> <br /> On top of that, in <i>The Shadow Over Innsmouth</i> the Esoteric Order of Dagon worships <b>both</b> Cthulhu and Dagon, but serve primarily Dagon, also worshiping Hydra as Dagon's wife. The only source I can remember that took this to equate Cthulhu and Dagon is <i>Cthulhu Tech</i>, which postdates Lovecraft by 70 years (almost exactly). Lovecraft refers to Dagon in several other works and it is <b>not</b> a name for Cthulhu.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486240#post1486240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Deep Ones are not worshiping Dagon the historical mythological figure, they are worshiping Cthulhu but applying (erroneously) the name of a god they're familiar with as a fundamentalist Christian educated town from the 19th century to early 20th.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how Lovecraft used to work.<br /> <br /> He either used names of his own creation, that could be entirely &quot;alien&quot; like Cthulhu or faux cultural names like Nyarlathotep (that he was certain to sound like Egyptian), or he used names from other cultures directly, at most creating faux etymologies for them from the alien-sounding names.<br /> <br /> In his works the &quot;elder&quot; cults had a sense of continuation, and when they somehow mixed with actual irl religion in any capacity it was in the opposite direction, their names and rituals were either directly more ancient than in reality or derivations of ancient forms, but not borrowed from &quot;normal&quot; religion, as happens with Nodens, Hypnos and Bast.<br /> <br /> Lovecraft wasn't a sensible author about culture and religion. He was deeply racist and unashamed about his prejudices even for a man of the 1920's, frequently drawing criticism to his narrow view of the world. When he wrote that a Mesopotamian deity was an alien demon or that most Pacific islanders were cannibals worshiping hellish deities, he fully meant it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486240#post1486240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My post is suggesting the Baali could be doing the same thing and adding the names of angels and other figures to alien things from beyond\u2122.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I just don't think they're the best way at all to do that. They're kind of too much on the nose and too threatening by themselves. When a Baali is found, you're probably going to be too focused on the fact there's a Baali in town to worry about entities that concern no one else than the Baali, and you already expect hellish rituals and demonic summoning anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T20:23:33-07:00","id":1486251,"title":"","content":"Something makes me wonder why Maynesylvania, I mean <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Massachutania, I mean Transylvania isn't a hotpot of endless Baali. Cuz hot damn, if that isn't the Lovecraft Country of WoD, I don't know what is (maybe the Middle-East). We got the mecca of Tzimisces (not only plenty of them, but the grandest: Damek, Velya, Vykos, Yorak, Noriz and Eldest themselves), the birthplace of the Vaulderie, a place where so much blood filled, the home of Dracula, and yeah, who could forget, GODDAMN KUPALA. But somehow it seems there isn't that many. And if Cathedral of Flesh isn't fleshy cthulhu material... We also get the home of the Tremere, and their abominations called Gargoyles.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I mean damn, we even get madmen in Octavinus and Dragomir. There is also the fact that for some goddamn question, Cappadocius decided to pop in there, in the middle of the Anarch Revolt, maybe for his Anointment, with a plan so insane it could work. And the Ante himself was a monstrous and unknowable thing or rational and profound thought. So yeah, we got our homeplace for Lovcraft in WoD.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T07:45:47-07:00","id":1486277,"title":"","content":"How about that - a thread I started years ago pops up again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486180#post1486180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No consider that, by the standards of Deep Time, vampires (at least according to Noddist thinking) are practically newborns. Assuming, of course, vampires are &quot;only&quot; 10,000 years old. A Lovecraftian Vampire campaign could easily challenge these assumptions, and present the idea that vampires, or their antecedents, have been around far longer than most can possibly imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree and this is a theme of Hunger from Beyond. In the book I write how the Jurado might be going on for 10k years. And so what of it\u2026 the Yith fought with the Flying Polyps for hundreds of millions of years. The horrors of the Mythos moves and operate across geological epochs.<br /> <br /> Edit: In my telling the Yith caused the KT Extinction Event as a move in their war against the Flying Polyps and other enemies. So the Yith spent millions of years to move an asteroid into place to hit the Earth, in an event which wiped out most of the then existing life on the planet and destroyed most of the then existing civilizations. Now, with that in mind, tell me again how impressive the Sabbat v. Camarillo war is?<br /> <br /> If I return to the subject I will probably link the Yith to the True Brujah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 07-12-2022, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T07:51:09-07:00","id":1486278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486251#post1486251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah, we got our homeplace for Lovcraft in WoD.[/SIZE][/COLOR][/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>And on a related note, the Revenant families have a Lovecraftian vibe to them; entire families of creepy weirdos that are the product of dubious breeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T07:59:39-07:00","id":1486279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486225#post1486225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lovecraftian themes aren't just about serving entities with weird names, it is about finding out that your entire society and world view is ultimately meaningless in the face of an uncaring universe whose span in space and time is unfathomable, inhabited by beings to whom we're less than a passing fad.</div> </div> </div> </div>To paraphrase the Quote from Game of Thrones, the night is dark and full of terrors\u2026 other than vampires.It\u2019s got things which make the most dire elder look trivial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T08:05:21-07:00","id":1486280,"title":"","content":"And my malicious\u2026I mean lovely book is available here; <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/382103/Hunger-from-Beyond-for-V5\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...-Beyond-for-V5</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 07-12-2022, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T11:08:27-07:00","id":1486296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486280#post1486280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And my malicious\u2026I mean lovely book is available here; <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/382103/Hunger-from-Beyond-for-V5\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...-Beyond-for-V5</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Fantastic book.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T12:28:38-07:00","id":1486305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486296#post1486296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fantastic book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you kindly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T09:41:01-07:00","id":1486433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486180#post1486180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No consider that, by the standards of Deep Time, vampires (at least according to Noddist thinking) are practically newborns. Assuming, of course, vampires are &quot;only&quot; 10,000 years old. A Lovecraftian Vampire campaign could easily challenge these assumptions, and present the idea that vampires, or their antecedents, have been around far longer than most can possibly imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of Deep Time and vampires; it\u2019s worth noting that recent archeological and paleontological finds have pushed the emerence of anatomically modern man back to at LEAST 300,000 years before present (i.e. long enough that we could fit all of our recorded history 60 times over into the amount of time modern humans have been around\u2026 and yet, even knowing how quickly all evidence of our civilization would crumble to nothing, we presume we\u2019re the first advanced civilization in all that span of time?) and the oldest structures (see G\u00f6bekli Tepe) to 9500 BCE and featuring sculpture far more advanced than we would see in the immediately periods.<br /> <br /> Lots of myths/folklore from around the world reference previous ages of men who were destroyed by calamity (even the Bible mentions a pre-flood iron-working civilization that would have been destroyed about the same time Atlantis was supposedly wiped out by the gods for its wickedness.<br /> <br /> Basically, you could easily extend vampires back into past forgotten civilizations; Atlantis, Mu, the Gold and Silver men of Greek Myth going back hundreds of thousands of years. Caine (if you want him to be the actual first vampire) could have sired and destroyed entire lines of vampires (excepting a few he missed who became the Sleepers like Namtaru) many times over\u2026 or Biblical Caine was actually the 31st (or 101st) Generation since Blood Caine (akin to Mitochondrial Eve; a hypothetical first vampire we may as well call Caine regardless of their actual gender for lack of any better name) and Namtaru and the other Sleepers are vampires so ancient that even the concept of humanity is alien to them.<br /> <br /> Hell, you could easily tie in the previous ages of KotE into the lost pre-history\u2026 entire civilizations rising even higher than our present one but then wiped away by the hundred thousand years since their fall.<br /> <br /> Vicissitude could be both vampiric and an \u201calien\u201d infection from a time so long ago that it may as well be an alien world and created by a vampire a dozen times more ancient than even Tzmisce (indeed, the Antediluvian may have just been that elder vampire\u2019s first victim in the \u201cmodern\u201d era.<br /> <br /> Ennoia tried to earthmeld to the center of the Earth and become one with Gaia\u2026 only to be consumed whole by a master of Protean whose already been there 50 times longer than she\u2019s been alivd.<br /> <br /> Maybe they are even the Neverborn\u2026 their dreams so ancient that they were carving their labyrinths in their dreams before the most recent time that man has rediscovered writing to record their existence.<br /> <br /> One hundred to two hundred millennia is so long that ANYONE still alive from back then would have to be alien beyond our understanding. Their plots and schemes span multiple rises and falls of civilizations\u2026 the entire rise and fall of Atlantis 12,000 years ago could be just an intermediate step in a gambit that won\u2019t reach fruition until AD 3000\u2026 and is just the equivalent of a \u201cfive year plan\u201d to us.<br /> <br /> Were Adam and Eve even the creations of God or an attempt by the Vicissitude ancient to recreate humanity after its childer had consumed them all in an attempt to grow a new food supply for itself and the curse spread to Caine to provide the food for a hunger beyond even the Methuselah\u2019s curse (the humans being just the food supply for the vampires it needs to eat)? How horrific do you want the truth to be?<br /> <br /> 300,000 years (that we have evidence for\u2026 who knows the actual number) is an unfathomable span of time in which all of recorded history is barely a speck\u2026 we don\u2019t even need lizard people to get to incomprehensible beings from before history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T10:03:02-07:00","id":1486437,"title":"","content":"The CALL OF CTHULHU game notes that both Deep Ones and Ghouls are actually far younger than the typical &quot;Old One&quot; or, say, the Yith. Part of the &quot;horror&quot; of Lovecraft is the fact that both the Deep Ones and ghouls are branches of humanity that evolved in parallel to humanity or were mutated by their association with the magic/weird science of the Great Old Ones. Humans themselves were created by the Elder Things but that gets a bit into continuity that HPL himself didn't really believe in.<br /> <br /> However, the reason ghouls and Deep Ones can breed with humans is, well, they are human.<br /> <br /> They are arguably a young race themselves and may have every bit as many mistakes about the nature of the Great Old Ones as humans (and while you may automatically dismiss this, in fact humans have quite a bit of knowledge about the Great Old Ones as the Cult of Cthulhu and academics as a whole have common access to the IDEAS behind them even if they're mostly ignorant as a whole).<br /> <br /> Another idea to consider is not just V:TM and Lovecraft but V:TM and Howard.<br /> <br /> It's a very different feel but might actually be easier as the realization that Enoch took place at the tail end of the Hyborian Age and wasn't even THAT important as Sorcerer Kingdoms ruled by monsters is a fairly common thing back then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T23:27:17-07:00","id":1486499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1273272-vtm-and-lovecraftian-themes?p=1486433#post1486433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it\u2019s worth noting that recent archeological and paleontological finds have pushed the emerence of anatomically modern man back to at LEAST 300,000 years before present (i.e. long enough that we could fit all of our recorded history 60 times over into the amount of time modern humans have been around\u2026 and yet, even knowing how quickly all evidence of our civilization would crumble to nothing, we presume we\u2019re the first advanced civilization in all that span of time?) and the oldest structures (see G\u00f6bekli Tepe) to 9500 BCE and featuring sculpture far more advanced than we would see in the immediately periods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have some things to say.<br /> <br /> First, before someone reaches the wrong conclusions, this is perfectly fine for fictional thought, but a little off from a real life standpoint. We can say for sure there was no other industrial civilization in the last 300.000 years because on that scale it would still leave a lot of surface and buried evidence, and even for longer time spans there are <i>some</i> evidence that we can pick up today. Although there is a possibility of a short-lived industrial civilization not being detectable by current methods after about 2 millions years, it is unlikely still. And our modern form isn't really likely to be far older than 300.000, while the initial 100.000 was a guesstimate at best, the current span isn't likely to be far off the mark.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, G\u00f6bekli Tepe <b>isn't</b> the oldest structure we've found, it is the oldest complex structure from the Neolithic, when those became relatively common indicating a species-wide change from nomadic to sedentary societies. <b>Actual</b> oldest structures go back another 10.000 years, they're just localized events and less likely to be permanent residences.<br /> <br /> Then we have the possibility of civilization under other species, which WoD already semi-recognizes in Werewolf. Other Homids shared the planet with us for most of our 300.000 years, and more predated us for more than 4 million years, beyond that 2 million magic mark. Before that we had other primates, a greater variety of mammals, dinosaurs and reptiles, and who knows what else could be civilization builders in the fictional past. We could have competing civilizations and sequences of civilizations.<br /> <br /> And with supernatural forces involved, how many of those could have left enduring abominations wandering the Earth? What if the Nictuku aren't a bunch of zealot 4th gens, but something stranger still? Maybe guardians of some buried secret the Nosferatu sometimes get too close to find, but at the same time they engendered the Nosferatu as a protection for this secret. They may well be Shoggoths as far as we know.<br /> <br /> What else could lie buried beneath the lands and oceans of a 5 billion years planet? What could come from the stars in a 14 billion years universe? What else could disguise as human so well that entities completely used to see the supernatural as human-derived wouldn't ever expect to exist? Which of the weirder things out there the main splats could be completely wrong about, and be older and more dangerous?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}